EXPERIMENT 24 – TEST DATA CREATION FOR TICKET BOOKING APPLICATION
AIM
To create test data for testing a ticket booking application using valid, invalid and boundary values for every input field.
ALGORITHM
1. List the booking form input fields: number of passengers, passenger age, travel date, travel class and payment mode.
2. Identify valid and invalid values using equivalence class partitioning.
3. Add boundary values for passengers (1–6), age (0–120) and travel date (within 120 days).
4. Prepare a test data table with data ID, field, value, type and expected result.
5. Specify the type, length, range and format of every field.
6. Create valid, boundary and invalid test data.
7. Execute the booking test cases and compare actual results with expected results.
INPUT
Field Specifications
Field	Rule
Passengers	1 to 6
Passenger age	0 to 120
Travel date	Today up to 120 days ahead
Travel class	SL, 3A, 2A, 1A
Mobile number	10 digits, starts with 6, 7, 8 or 9
E-mail	Valid format with one @ and a domain
Payment mode	Card, UPI or Net banking

Test Data
Data ID	Field	Test Data	Type	Expected Result
TD01	Passengers	0	Invalid	Minimum 1 passenger
TD02	Passengers	1	Valid	Booking page displayed
TD03	Passengers	6	Valid	Booking page displayed
TD04	Passengers	7	Invalid	Maximum 6 passengers
TD05	Passenger age	4	Valid	Fare = 0
TD06	Passenger age	-1	Invalid	Enter a valid age
TD07	Travel date	Yesterday	Invalid	Date cannot be in the past
TD08	Travel date	Today + 120 days	Valid	Seats displayed
TD09	Travel date	Today + 121 days	Invalid	Booking is not open
TD10	Travel class	SL / AC	Valid	Fare of the class displayed
TD11	Payment mode	Card / UPI / Net banking	Valid	Payment page displayed
TD12	Payment mode	None selected	Invalid	Select the payment mode
TD13	Passenger age	120	Valid	Booking page displayed
TD14	Passenger age	121	Invalid	Enter a valid age

OUTPUT
Test Execution Summary
Total Designed	Executed	Passed	Failed	Blocked	Pass %
14	14	14	0	0	100%

RESULT
Thus, the test data of the ticket booking application was created using equivalence classes and boundary values, and the output was verified. Valid, invalid and boundary values were prepared for every field.
